{
  "version": 1,
  "recorded_utc": "2026-10-30T15:11:07.824364+00:00",
  "scope": "Phase four: flags parameter editing in lists, native dialogs and nested structures",
  "status": "Implemented and validated on macOS arm64 Release; phase four remains in progress.",
  "implemented": [
    "Flags reuse ParameterValue integer storage and the existing C interface version 12. Labels and masks are copied through the same metadata fields as other selectable parameter values; no public SDK, STL, SDL or ImGui types are added.",
    "parameter.flags, parameter.flags-value, parameter.flags-set and value.flags use the ordinary property, query, command and renderer registration. Built-in and independent module implementations use the same entry points.",
    "All 32 value bits are retained, including the sign bit and unlisted bits. Zero and combined choice masks remain in the projection. The native dialog preserves its single-bit layout and compact text; inline controls preserve their flag list and combined-mask behavior.",
    "The former inline SetParameterBytes branch and native dialog mask lookup/write branch are removed. The dialog obtains dimensions from its captured query provider and renders through its selected value editor.",
    "Updates change only the working value. Acceptance creates one undo record; cancellation and unchanged values preserve the document, Dirty and Redo. Escape during a held checkbox clears its active input so release cannot write a delayed toggle.",
    "Flags participate in recursive structure editing and undo without replacing member instances. A native working parameter is edited without changing its source or history.",
    "An independently compiled module replaces the flag query, renderer and modifier. An open dialog continues using its captured choices after configuration switches back.",
    "No SDK or viewport rendering/transfer implementation changed."
  ],
